    "title": "Google Gmail and Calendar arrive as first-class org integrations",
    "intro": "Today's nightly is focused on a single, sizable shipped capability: connecting Aura to Google. Users can now link Gmail and Calendar through the org integrations surface, backed by a new trusted-runtime path on the server and an overhauled integration editor in the interface.",
    "entries": [
      {
        "batch_id": "entry-1",
        "time_label": "2:54 PM",
        "started_at": "2026-06-06T21:54:55.000Z",
        "ended_at": "2026-06-06T21:54:55.000Z",
        "title": "Google Gmail and Calendar integration",
        "summary": "Aura can now connect to a user's Google account and expose Gmail and Calendar as org tools, with end-to-end support across the server, integrations crate, and settings UI.",
        "items": [
          {
            "text": "Users can connect Gmail and Calendar from Org Settings → Integrations via a new Google OAuth flow proxied through aura-integrations, with the required AURA_INTEGRATIONS_URL wiring documented in the README and .env.example.",
            "commit_shas": [
              "0f3fce7a931bb01eae7d522dca1d2bdc4aa8f0f9"
            ],
            "confidence": "high"
          },
          {
            "text": "A new trusted-runtime module and Google trusted methods (~340 lines in trusted_methods/google.rs plus helpers) back the Gmail and Calendar tool calls server-side, with integration_actions and provider mock tests covering the path.",
            "commit_shas": [
              "0f3fce7a931bb01eae7d522dca1d2bdc4aa8f0f9"
            ],
            "confidence": "high"
          },
          {
            "text": "Org tool dispatch now carries the authenticated user's identity into provider calls, tightening ownership so Google actions execute against the connecting user rather than the org generically — every provider handler (Apify, Brave, Buffer, Freepik, GitHub, Linear, Mailchimp, Metricool, Notion, Resend, Slack) was updated to the new signature.",
            "commit_shas": [
              "0f3fce7a931bb01eae7d522dca1d2bdc4aa8f0f9"
            ],
            "confidence": "high"
          },
          {
            "text": "The Integration Editor and Org Settings Integrations panel were substantially reworked (~300 lines in IntegrationEditor, ~170 in OrgSettingsIntegrations) and covered by a new google-integration-ui Playwright spec, giving the Google connect/disconnect experience a dedicated UI surface.",
            "commit_shas": [
              "0f3fce7a931bb01eae7d522dca1d2bdc4aa8f0f9"
            ],
            "confidence": "high"
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "highlights": [
      "Gmail and Calendar connectable via Google OAuth",
      "New trusted-runtime path for Google tool calls",
      "Integration editor reworked for per-user ownership"
    ],
